.TH HAPIQ-FETCH-MAGNET 1 "" "hapiq" "hapiq manual"
.SH NAME
hapiq-fetch-magnet \- BitTorrent transfer helper for hapiq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hapiq-fetch-magnet
.br
.B hapiq-fetch-magnet seed
.B \-\-cache-dir
.I DIR
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR HOST:PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-advertise
.IR HOST:PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-tracker
.IR URLS ]
.br
.B hapiq-fetch-magnet tracker
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR ADDR ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-trust-proxy ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches and seeds blobs of a hapiq cache over BitTorrent.
.BR hapiq (1)
finds it on
.B PATH
and starts it itself; without it, hapiq downloads from the peer cache or the
origin URL as before.
Every blob fetched this way is checked against its sha256 by hapiq.
.PP
With no arguments it reads fetch requests as JSON lines on standard input and
answers on standard output.
This mode is for hapiq, not for people.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B seed
Serve every blob in a hapiq cache and write one magnet per blob to
.IR DIR /magnets/<sha256>,
which
.B hapiq cache serve
hands out to peers. The magnets are removed on exit.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-cache-dir " DIR"
hapiq cache directory (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST:PORT"
BitTorrent listen address (default 0.0.0.0:42069).
.TP
.BI \-\-advertise " HOST:PORT"
Address other nodes dial, written into every magnet (default:
.BR \-\-listen ).
Must not be 0.0.0.0 or [::].
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " DURATION"
How often to rescan for new blobs (default 30s).
.TP
.BI \-\-tracker " URLS"
Comma-separated tracker announce URLs (default:
.BR $HAPIQ_MAGNET_TRACKERS ).
.RE
.TP
.B tracker
Run an in-memory HTTP tracker that seeders and fetchers find each other
through. Run it on the cache's host.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " ADDR"
HTTP listen address (default :6969).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " DURATION"
Re-announce interval handed to clients (default 2m).
.TP
.B \-\-trust-proxy
Take the client address from the last X-Forwarded-For entry. Only behind a
reverse proxy that sets it.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HAPIQ_MAGNET_LISTEN
Listen address when fetching (default 0.0.0.0:0).
.TP
.B HAPIQ_MAGNET_TIMEOUT
Give up after this long without metadata or new bytes (default 30s).
.TP
.B HAPIQ_MAGNET_TRACKERS
Default for
.BR "seed \-\-tracker" .
.TP
.B HAPIQ_MAGNET_VERBOSE
If set, report on standard error which peers each file came from.
.TP
.B HAPIQ_MAGNET_DEBUG
If set, also dump the torrent client's state on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hapiq (1),
.BR hapiq-cache-serve (1)
.PP
https://github.com/btraven00/hapiq/tree/main/helpers/hapiq-fetch-magnet
